Name: Rana Haider saleem
reg no: 24-cs-003

START
1. Set initial output Q = 0.
2. Display the input controls.
3. Ask the user to select a flip-flop type.
4. If D Flip-Flop is selected:
   Read D input.
   Wait for the Clock button.
   When Clock is pressed:
   Set Next Q = D.
   Update Q.
5. If JK Flip-Flop is selected:
   Read J and K inputs.
   Wait for the Clock button.
   When Clock is pressed:
      If J = 0 and K = 0:
      Keep previous Q.
      If J = 0 and K = 1:
      Set Q = 0.
      If J = 1 and K = 0:
      Set Q = 1.
      If J = 1 and K = 1:
      Change Q to its opposite value.
6. Display the new Q output.
7. Add the clock number, inputs and Q output
   to the history table.
8. Repeat whenever the Clock button is pressed.
9. Stop when the user closes the simulator.
END
